              "text": "lēctor, lēctōris — \"a reader\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Lēctor dominō librum legit. The reader reads a book to his master."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Masculine, third declension, from legō. Rich houses kept a slave to read aloud."
            }
          ]
        },
