              "text": "ēvolvō, ēvolvere — \"to unroll; to read (a book)\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Discipulus librum ēvolvit et legit. The pupil unrolls the book and reads."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ēvolvō, ēvolvere, ēvolvī, ēvolūtum. Books were rolls, so to read was to unroll. English evolve."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ēvolvō is built on ē- \"out\" and volvō \"to roll\" (EtymDB; Lewis & Short): to unroll a book. English evolve comes from it."
            }
          ]
        },
